<div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1531170-have-the-pelagials-made-any-appearances-in-3e?p=1531178#post1531178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sunken Luthe was covered in <b>Lunars: Fangs at the Gate</b>, but <b>Across the Eight Directions</b> doesn't go down into the depths of the West at all.<br /> <br /> However, AtED does have a nice section on the Lintha and Bluehaven.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good to know, guess it's more than time for me to get that one.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-20T06:13:19-08:00","id":1531189,"title":"","content":"Last I heard there was talk that they might get a new name due to the potentially confusing similarity to the also aquatic but fundamentally human Pelagothropes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12844-bladewind","name":"Bladewind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-20T06:44:24-08:00","id":1531191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bladewind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1531170-have-the-pelagials-made-any-appearances-in-3e?p=1531189#post1531189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last I heard there was talk that they might get a new name due to the potentially confusing similarity to the also aquatic but fundamentally human Pelagothropes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes, i never had much of an issue with that - always parsed the later as &quot;Pelagic-<i>anthropes</i>&quot; in my head, what kind of helped i guess - but i'm aware it has been a source of frequent confusion amidst the fanbase, so can see the sense in doing so.<br /> <br /> One thing i do hope for is some bit of variation, both physically - while manatees are cited as a comparison to Pelagials' lower bodies, so are seals and truth be told most of their characteristics seem to harken more to pinnipeds overall, imho - and socio-culturally (their original write-up in Creatures of the Wyld having much that could stand fine on its own apart to their 2e with the Sleeping Princes &amp; related narrative).<br /> <br /> Now that i think of it, tribes or ethnic groups among them with visual elements or little nods taken from manatees, pinnipeds and/or cetaceans could be entertaining from a visual/descriptive standpoint too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}